# ============================================================================
#  windOS Zen — 05-kernel-liquorix.list.chroot
#  Kernel shootout: Liquorix (Zen-tuned) instead of the stock Debian kernel.
#
#  Repo is trixie (verified: https://liquorix.net/debian/dists/trixie/ ships
#  linux-image-liquorix-amd64 7.2-18.1~trixie), pulled via
#  config/archives/liquorix.list.chroot.
#
#  Unqualified names: apt picks the highest version from the one enabled
#  third-party suite. No release qualification is used because Liquorix has
#  no -backports/-updates suites.
#
#  NOTE: --linux-flavours liquorix-amd64 in auto/config makes live-build's own
#  chroot_linux-image schedule linux-image-liquorix-amd64, so the stock Debian
#  kernel is never pulled in. Only ONE vmlinuz-* exists, which keeps the
#  globs in binary_grub_cfg ("basename chroot/boot/vmlinuz-*${DEFAULT_FLAVOUR}"
#  => *liquorix-amd64) and binary_syslinux single-valued. The entries below are
#  kept for explicitness; apt dedupes against the flavour-scheduled image.
#  Do NOT set --linux-packages none to achieve this: that also short-circuits
#  binary_linux-image (chroot_archives stage 24), which is the step that copies
#  vmlinuz/initrd into binary/live/, so the ISO ends up with no kernel.
# ============================================================================
linux-image-liquorix-amd64
linux-headers-liquorix-amd64